<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Dec copper, lead output up, zinc down.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Dec copper, lead output up, zinc down.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakh copper output rose by 14.5 percent in December 1996 on the previous month, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Over the same period, zinc production fell by 2.2 percent, while lead production rose by 9.4 percent.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following figures for non-ferrous metals production, in tonnes, with percentage changes below -</p>
<p>					 Dec 96    Nov 96    Jan-Dec 96</p>
<p> Copper				21,717    18,973     267,140</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     +14.5     +7.5	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     -14.7    -19.3	  +4.5</p>
<p> Zinc				   15,309   15,650     170,351</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		-2.2     +2.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +21.1    +13.1	  +0.7</p>
<p> Lead				    6,378    5,829	67,270</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		+9.4     +8.8	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +67.8    +17.7	 -24.0</p>
<p> Bauxite			     304,300  267,500   3,344,900</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	     +13.8     -4.5	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change		+8.9    +10.6	  +0.8</p>
<p> Alumina				93,974   91,027   1,083,476</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		+3.2     -3.2	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change		+0.9     +2.7	  +5.8</p>
<p> Titanium				1,212    1,239	12,458</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change		-2.2     +9.0	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	     +25.6    +34.7	 +29.9</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
